# DNS UPDATE ingress for DNS injection. dnsmasq owns every gateway's :53 and
# does not implement RFC 2136, so this diverts only UPDATE-opcode packets to
# the daemon's per-profile listeners and leaves the query dataplane untouched
# — if the daemon is down, UPDATEs fail and nothing else does.
#
# The UDP header is 64 bits, the DNS flags byte starts at bit 80, so the
# 4-bit opcode is `@th,81,4`; 5 is UPDATE. The client is UDP-only, so there
# is no TCP variant (TCP DNS's length prefix makes the offset non-constant).
#
# `fib daddr type local` confines the divert to UPDATEs addressed to the
# router itself: without it the rule also catches UPDATEs merely transiting
# to an external authoritative server — ddns-scripts' nsupdate backend does
# exactly that. `redirect` (not `dnat`) preserves the destination address and
# rewrites only the port, so one static ruleset serves every profile gateway
# and replies un-NAT through conntrack. Priority -101 beats fw4's own dstnat
# chain (-100) — netfilter orders base chains by declared priority — so the
# per-profile DNS-Override DNAT never sees a diverted packet, and stays above
# conntrack (-200). The rate limits shed an UPDATE flood before the daemon
# pays for parse + TSIG + directory lookup per packet.
#
# Two target ports because the daemon binds each listener to exactly one
# kernel device (that is what closes cross-segment source spoofing): inbound
# WireGuard arrivals go to the wg-bound listeners on one port, everything
# else to the bridge-bound listeners on another, so no two sockets ever share
# an (addr, port) pair. `redirect` is terminal, so the first matching rule
# wins.
#
# `redirect` needs kmod-nft-nat; without that package fw4 fails to load the
# ENTIRE ruleset, so this file and the kmod-nft-nat entry in
# build/openwrt.diffconfig must ship together.
chain startwrt_dns_update_divert {
	type nat hook prerouting priority -101; policy accept;
	iifname "wg_*" meta nfproto ipv4 fib daddr type local udp dport 53 @th,81,4 == 5 limit rate 20/second burst 50 packets counter redirect to :9554
	meta nfproto ipv4 fib daddr type local udp dport 53 @th,81,4 == 5 limit rate 20/second burst 50 packets counter redirect to :9553
}
